// Package repository is where this service talks to the outside world:
// databases, caches, other services' APIs.
//
// Belongs here: implementations of the interfaces declared by
// internal/service, the SQL or client calls behind them, and the translation
// of a driver's errors into the domain taxonomy in internal/apierror.
//
// Does NOT belong here: business rules — a repository that decides whether an
// operation is allowed has taken a decision away from the service layer — and
// HTTP types. A driver error must never escape this package unwrapped; a
// caller upstack cannot distinguish "row not found" from "connection
// refused" once it is an opaque error, but this package can.
//
// Empty until Mint chunk 07.
package repository
